"ion errors |\\n| `force_settle(channel_id, final_root, aggregate_gn, claimed_measured_root, agent_receipt_sig, transcript_ref, verified_turns)` | miner or agent (signed) | verify the same receipt/turn/claim gates; compute two-part tariff `P`; open challenge window | receipt/turn/root/claim errors; rejects `P > E` with `TariffExceedsEscrow` (R12.1d) |\\n| `finalize(channel_id)` | anyone (signed) | after the challenge window, pay `P` \u2192 miner, `(1\u2212\u03c6)(E\u2212P)` \u2192 agent, `\u03c6(E\u2212P)` \u2192 burn/Foundation; `P` is in the escrow's base unit (10\u207b\u00b9\u2078 FLOP), with `channel_base_per_turn = rate_G = 1` base unit | window not elapsed; open dispute |\\n| `timeout(channel_id)` | anyone (signed) | non-delivery \u2192 full refund (`\u03c6=0`) | not past `max_duration` |\\n| `open_dispute(channel_id, contested_turn)` | session agent or active validator | lock [`channel_challenger_bond`](#param-channel_challenger_bond); contest one settled turn, which the miner answers with `respond_dispute` | `NoDisputeStanding`; `DisputeTurnNotSettled`; `DisputeExists`; window elapsed; transcript unavailable |\\n| `open_bisection_dispute(channel_id, n_turns)` | session agent or active validator | lock the challenger bond; `n_turns` equals the settled power-of-two leaf count (2 to `MaxSettlementTurns`); begin midpoint rounds over the whole bundle | `BisectionBadTurnCount`; `DisputeTurnNotSettled`; standing and window errors as `open_dispute` |\\n| `respond_bisection(channel_id, left_root, right_root)` | named miner (signed) | open the two child roots, whose hash equals the interval's parent root; reset the response window | `NotAParty`; `BisectionNotAwaitingResponse`; `BisectionBadChildRoots`; window elapsed |\\n| `challenge_bisection(channel_id, choose_left)` | the dispute's challenger | pick the left or right half; once one turn remains, the miner answers with `respond_dispute` | `NotAParty`; `BisectionNotAwaitingChallenge`; `BisectionRoundCap`; window elapsed |\\n| `respond_dispute(channel_id, leaf_version, turn_index, h_in, h_out, g_n, decode_policy_hash, h_ids, toploc_commitment_hash, miner_recv_ms, miner_done_ms, latency_ms, enclave_sig, merkle_path)` | miner (signed) | select exactly one Appendix F leaf preimage; verify signature + Merkle membership | unsupported version; bad signature/path; window elapsed \u2192 fraud default |\\n| `report_toploc_mismatch(channel_id, evidence)` | active validator | quorum-judged activation mismatch \u2192 forgery slash | uncalibrated cell (fail-closed inert) |\\n\\n### G.2 PoUI direct rail \u2014 `pallet_flop_poui` (synthetic/ghost/calibration/simulator, \u00a73.6)\\n\\n| Extrinsic | Origin | Effect |\\n|-----------|--------|--------|\\n| `submit_stark_batch(proofs, gn_weight, task_hash, latency_ms, model_hash, output_hash)` | miner (signed) | record in `PendingVerifications`; replay-guard `ProcessedTasks[task_hash]` |\\n| `submit_validator_attestations(bundle)` | none (unsigned inherent; `ensure_none`) \u2014 validator identity authenticated by the signatures inside the bundle, not the extrinsic origin | verify sigs + active-validator check + tuple agreement + quorum; on quorum verify `report_data`/`output_hash`, credit `gn_weight`, fire `OnProofVerified` |\\n| `set_validator_attestation_threshold(perbill)` | root/governance | set the BFT quorum fraction |\\n\\n### G.3 Staking, calibration, vesting, DA, HTLC\\n\\n| Extrinsic | Pallet | Effect |\\n|-----------|--------|--------|\\n| `register_miner(commission)` / unbond | `miner_staking` | bond \u2265 capacity-proportional requirement (\u00a76.1); slash-locked unbond |\\n| `register` / `rotate` / `do_slash` | `validators` | self-stake register \u2192 queue; stake-ordered rotation; single slash authority |\\n| `accept_benchmark_burst(...)` / `renew_benchmark_cap(...)` | `hw_calibration` | stake-backed aggregate cap / lease renewal |\\n| `claim_vested()` | `airdrop_vesting`; beneficiary (signed) | use the finalized head; require an existing grant and positive unlocked amount above `claimed`; reduce the grant freeze and emit `AirdropClaimed`; errors `NoGrant`, `NothingToClaim` |\\n| `update_miner_performance(miner, mainnet_performance)` | `airdrop_vesting`; Root | require a Miner grant, a testnet baseline, and positive mainnet score; update the score and emit `MinerPerformanceUpdated`; errors `NoGrant`, `InvalidPerformanceScore` |\\n| `record_attested_gpu_inventory(...)` / `record_hardware_fingerprint(...)` | `hw_calibration` | identity binding; change invalidates |\\n| `batch_issue_calibration_jobs(...)` | `synthetic_tasks` | issuer-selected timed one-shot pack |\\n| `create_grant(miner, amount)` | `work_vesting` | Root only; require the miner's non-zero finalized \u00a77 calibration baseline and snapshot it as `B_p` (R8.1) |\\n| `force_create_grant(miner, amount, pledge_baseline)` | `work_vesting` | Root only; explicitly bypass the finalized calibration-baseline check with a non-zero caller-supplied `B_p` (R8.1) |\\n| `register_miner(model_hash, gpu_model, vram_gb, tee_type)` / `set_measured_root` | `model_registry` | model availability + measured dm-verity root |\\n| DA register / audit / `top_up_lease` / `withdraw_lease(commitment)` | `da_registry` | `DataRef` commitment; serve-or-slash audit; free lease top-up; `withdraw_lease`: publisher (signed); requires an existing `Leased` blob, matching publisher, and `pin_count == 0`, with no `lease_end` condition; removes the blob (no further audits can be issued) and refunds the full deposit to the publisher; does not cancel an audit issued before withdrawal (E.47); errors `UnknownBlob`, `NotLeased`, `NotPublisher`, `BlobPinned`; emits `LeaseWithdrawn`, `LeaseDepositRefunded` |\\n| `create/redeem/refund_htlc`, `create_cross_chain_htlc`, `relay_preimage`, `register_relayer` | `has-station` | HTLC lifecycle (\u00a710); permissioned relayer |\\n| session-key / agent-wallet delegation, caps, revoke | `session_keys` / `agent_wallet` | \u00a76.2 delegated autonomy |\\n\\n---\\n\\n### G.4 Paid object storage (\u00a75.4)\\n\\n**R5.4p \u2014 Interface pinning.** These are logical interfaces; E.54 **MUST** pin bounded wire types and dispatch indices before\\nactivation. Every call **MUST** reject an inactive/unknown profile. Events **MUST** include affected\\nreservation/lane/object identifiers and accounting deltas without private contents or keys.\\n\\n| Signature | Origin | Preconditions / principal errors | Event |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| `vote_tariff(epoch, tariff)` | eligible validator | next epoch not yet started; counted only with a capacity declaration; duplicate / ineligible | `TariffVoteRecorded` |\\n| `declare_capacity(epoch, encoded_bytes)` | eligible validator | collateral available under the E.54 bond profile; not reused across obligations; ineligible / insufficient collateral | `CapacityDeclared` |\\n| `open_reservation(reserved_bytes, term, max_cost, nonce)` | payer | valid capabilities, funds for `C_rent` at the current tariff within `max_cost`, free declared capacity; unauthorized / insufficient budget or capacity | `ReservationPending`; `ReservationActivated` by protocol assignment at the next finalized randomness, or `ReservationAborted` with escrow returned |\\n| `extend_reservation(reservation, additional_term, max_cost)` | authorized funded renewer | fresh consent at the funding epoch's tariff, providers' declared capacity; closed / insufficient budget | `ReservationExtended` |\\n| `transfer_reservation(reservation, new_payer, consent)` | owner with new payer's signed acceptance | active reservation, no pending transfer; unauthorized / claims pending | `ReservationTransferred`; terms, providers and liability unchanged |\\n| `set_memory_head(namespace, key, expected_version, new_object)` | owner or scoped writer | optional chain-pinned slow path; exact previous version (chain-pinned or quorum-receipted); stale head / unauthorized | `MemoryHeadPinned`; authoritative for that key over provider receipts |\\n| `post_checkpoint(epoch, root, counters_commitment)` | assigned validator | one per provider per epoch within grace; duplicate / late / conflicting | `CheckpointPosted`; late or missing after grace is a fault |\\n| *(protocol action, no extrinsic)* rent release per epoch | block execution | historical slot holder's audit and checkpoint state accepted for the interval; challenge window elapsed; uncredited term positions; per-slot/tranche `R_sk(b) \u2212 R_sk(a)` only; checked arithmetic | `RentReleased` to the interval's holder, including after replacement |\\n| `challenge_storage(reservation, generation, evidence)` | profile-authorized challenger; anyone for equivocation | objective evidence: failed audit, missing custody receipt after the activation window, missing checkpoint after grace, or conflicting receipts/checkpoints; applicable bond/standing; stale assignment / invalid evidence | `StorageChallenged`; profile-bound `RepairAssigned` / `StorageFault` / `EquivocationSlashed` |\\n| `finalize_reservation(reservation)` | any caller, for an expired or failed reservation | finalized cause-bound end; only after bounded claims and liabilities close; settle surviving historical rent entitlements; no live holds; checked per-slot refund `\u03a3_k B_sk \u2212 paid \u2212 held`; claims pending | `ReservationClosed`, fault remedy where applicable, failed/unserved/forfeited rent and surplus returned to payer, prune authorization |\\n| `set_object_policy(namespace, expected_epoch, policy_commitment)` | owner | monotonic finalized epoch and bounded policy; stale epoch / unauthorized | `ObjectPolicyUpdated` |\\n| `fund_service_lane(reservation, provider, budget, nonce)` | payer | assigned provider, fresh nonce, aggregate wallet cap and held funds; unauthorized / over budget | `ServiceLaneFunded` |\\n| `redeem_service(lane, voucher)` | lane's provider, directly or through an authorized proxy dispatching as the provider; fixed payee | signature/domain/range; strictly increasing sequence and nondecreasing counters; exact pinned-tariff amount above paid and within budget; Closing requires known finalized height \u2264 deadline regardless of signing time; only the cumulative delta; replay / overclaim / expired claim / unknown clock | `ServicePaid` |\\n| `close_service_lane(lane)` / `finalize_service_lane(lane)` | payer to close; any caller to finalize | fixed boundary at close inclusion or earlier reservation end; pinned deadline = boundary + claim window; preserve slot and escrow; refund exactly remaining escrow only with known finalized height > deadline; unauthorized / claims pending / unknown clock | `ServiceLaneClosing` / `ServiceLaneClosed` |\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Appendix H \u2014 Conformance & Implementation-Status Matrix\\n\\nThe single home for **implementation status** (kept out of the normative body, \u00a70). Status legend:\\n`LIVE` implemented \u00b7 `PARTIAL` partly implemented \u00b7 `PLANNED` designed, not wired \u00b7 `GAP`\\nunhandled/unspecified \u00b7 `OOS` out of protocol scope by design. This appendix is informative and tracks\\nthe codebase; the normative *requirement* is always the cited section.\\n\\n### H.1 Core protocol\\n\\n| Requirement / mechanism | \u00a7 | Status |\\n|-------------------------|---|--------|\\n| Public claim evidence | \u00a70 | PENDING: private Lean/Quint bundle reproduced under named hypotheses; public source/run bundle awaits a software-license grant; implementation refinement and empirical evidence remain open |\\n| BABE authoring + AlephBFT finality (1 s blocks) | \u00a72 | LIVE |\\n| Per-rotation VRF committee sampling | \u00a72.3, \u00a715.4 | LIVE draw; \u2264100 pool returns all; stake-only fallback drops recency whenever no active validator clears both the stake floor and recency (including every recent-work validator below the floor); capture/min-size proof GAP (E.42) |\\n| Verification-liveness committee gate (R2.4, R15.4c) | \u00a72.3, \u00a715.4 | PLANNED: recency still written from prover credit only (`ValidatorWorkRecorder` credits the submitter of a verified PoUI proof); no protocol-issued duties; no attestation client (E.52). Until wired, only an account that also mines passes recency, paying the miner capacity bond and credit cap (\u00a72.4), so the \u00a72.3 stake-only committee cost does not yet hold |\\n| Committee Sybil capital: self-stake vs backing | \u00a72.3, \u00a715.2 | GAP: the committee gate compares `total_stake` (self + delegated + sponsored) with `effective_minimum_stake()`, and that backing is not locked as distinct capital (`delegate` freezes without a balance check; `sponsor_validator` checks each tranche with `reducible_balance(.., Force)`, which ignores existing freezes; freezes overlap rather than add). Self-stake is floor-checked at `register`/`rejoin` and from the recorded bond at queue promotion; `MinSelfStakeRatio` is checked only when backing is added, and a liveness slash charges self-stake first while `un_jail` restores without a re-check (E.42) |\\n| Queued validator self-stake top-up | \u00a715.2, \u00a715.5 | GAP: `register` bonds exactly the effective minimum; extra free balance does not increase recorded self-stake. `rejoin` tops up only extended-downtime-kicked validators, so a queued candidate below a raised floor remains deferred until the floor falls or registration is replaced. Backing admission is bounded by recorded self-stake |\\n| Three safety sub-proofs | \u00a72.3 | GAP: seat-capture/undersized/bootstrap bridge open (E.42) |\\n| GHOSTDAG/PoW fork removed; GRANDPA removed | \u00a72 | LIVE |\\n\\n### H.2 Verification (\u00a73)\\n\\n| Requirement / mechanism | Status |\\n|-------------------------|--------|\\n| TEE attestation (DCAP/dstack), quote \u2192 `report_data` | LIVE (on-TDX e2e pending) |\\n| Measured `model_hash` \u2014 reproducible packer + registry-root gate + verifier RTMR3 parse | LIVE (CVM RTMR3 extension PLANNED) |\\n| Output binding (`output_hash`) + decode-policy binding | LIVE |\\n| TOPLOC Tier 2 (commitment required; end-to-end error bound open) | PARTIAL |\\n| Tier 3 re-execution / session dispute game | PARTIAL |\\n| Re-execution checker lane (R3.5d: checkers re-run, validators verify + co-sign) | PLANNED: shipped checker re-prefills inside the validator watchtower (E.53) |\\n| Tier 4 validator BFT quorum crediting | LIVE |\\n| Canonical wire/rejection profile + public Rust/TS/Python vectors | PARTIAL: formats/vectors LIVE; task-domain producer/validator enforcement and legacy receipt resume profile open (E.51) |\\n| TEE-optional reframe (TEE-independent floor; TEE = optional HARD tier) | DECIDED |\\n| Non-TEE (SOFT) settlement lane end-to-end | PARTIAL: SOFT calibration entry, non-attested model onboarding (`flop model onboard --soft`) and persistent non-TEE session signing keys landed; miner registration still requires a `TeeType`; spot-check rate, demand-floor exclusion and checker-lane disputes open |\\n\\n### H.3 Metering, sizing, DA (\u00a74\u2013\u00a75)\\n\\n| Requirement / mechanism | Status |\\n|-------------------------|--------|\\n| Reference-work `G_n` accounting engine (MoE + attention, KAT-pinned) | LIVE |\\n| Runtime emission of reference-work `g_n` into `report_data` | LIVE |\\n| Reject-only throughput tripwire | LIVE |\\n| Per-GPU MLPerf ceiling / under-report floor | PARTIAL |\\n| `G_n` integer unit taxonomy | LIVE: wire/settlement checks; the reference meter, RISC0 audit guest and SDKs reject out-of-width values instead of clamping |\\n| Cache-aware settlement discount | PLANNED |\\n| Sovereign DA \u2014 on-chain protocol + `DataRef` plumbing | LIVE |\\n| DA availability, anti-grinding, repair and retention budget | GAP \u2014 PENDING E.47 |\\n| DA audits outstanding at lease withdrawal or prune | GAP \u2014 PENDING E.47 |\\n| Sovereign DA \u2014 off-chain validator service (RS encode/serve/audit) | PARTIAL |\\n| Protocol DA duty; serve-or-slash; leased weights + refundable deposit (\u00a75.3) | LIVE |\\n| Paid encrypted agent objects, memory heads, capabilities, storage escrow, and retrieval vouchers (\u00a75.4) | PARTIAL on development networks only (R5.4q): the `paid-storage` pallet runs at runtime index 108 behind the devnet-only `paid-storage-unratified` feature, with the da-validator paid data plane and the TypeScript SDK; rent is released without a custody audit (`UnratifiedNoAudit`). Production ACTIVATION BLOCKED by E.54/E.47 |\\n| Paid-storage Lean accounting, authority, and historical-liability invariants (\u00a75.4) | PARTIAL: unbounded draft contracts and countermodels; slot/tranche rounding ratified by D-0524; full composition and runtime conformance PENDING |\\n| Paid-storage Quint lifecycle, adversary, and conformance models (\u00a75.4) | PARTIAL: lifecycle, authority, admission, rent and lane models run in CI (sampled invariants, not exhaustive); runtime refinement PENDING |\\n| Paid-storage agent/validator market and solvency simulation (\u00a75.4) | PARTIAL: TypeScript and Julia storage-market and validator-solvency models with seeded scenario results; not a launch tariff (tariff ratification #1565) |\\n| Reorg-safe indexer serving (finalized prefix) | PARTIAL |\\n\\n### H.4 Primitives, calibration, vesting, emission (\u00a76\u2013\u00a79)\\n\\n| Requirement / mechanism | Status |\\n|-------------------------|--------|\\n| balances/multisig/proxy/staking/delegation/vesting | LIVE |\\n| Capacity-proportional miner self-stake (linear, no cap) | LIVE (value provisional) |\\n| Declarative spend-condition layer; N-party escrow; capabilities | PARTIAL |\\n| Agent session keys + caps + circuit breaker | LIVE (breaker trip latch PARTIAL: rolled back with the rejected call, R6.2c) |\\n| 10-minute benchmark entry (SOFT/HARD), deposit-first | LIVE |\\n| Multi-GPU `(SKU,count)` inventory + aggregate HARD ceiling | LIVE |\\n| Seven-day lease; restart/expiry renewal supervisor | LIVE |\\n| Timed issuer-selected calibration packs | LIVE |\\n| Legacy three-phase dyno | REMOVED |\\n| Statistical rolling degradation/downshift | PLANNED |\\n| Drift: EWMA/control charts + MLPerf ceiling | PLANNED |\\n| Performance-locked vesting `R_p\u00b2` + blackout | LIVE (Root `force_create_grant` bypasses the \u00a77 baseline) |\\n| Era-T conversion snapshot and per-cohort allocation (\u00a78.2) | PARTIAL (cohort pools enforced; completed-job and active-day weights removed, as R8.4 requires; score caps and aggregation open in E.38) |\\n| Genesis airdrop funding and grants (\u00a78.2) | PARTIAL (genesis bridge absent; existing grant calls mint) |\\n| Airdrop claims, unlock schedule, and locked compute spend (\u00a78.2 R8.7, R8.8) | PARTIAL (claims use finality and locked compute spend is wired; the pallet still vests every tier linearly with the retired miner performance adjustment and `update_miner_performance`, and lets any tier spend locked principal; no genesis quarter, earn-to-unlock credit, or Validator freeze and daily release; no Agent spend credit or spend cap, and compute-channel refunds re-freeze up to the locked principal a channel drew, without applying R8.8's payable-first draw. Miner self-stake over a still-frozen grant rides on overlapping `AirdropVesting` and `MinerSelfStake` freezes, but `miner-slashing` and `validators` lower only their own stake freeze before transferring proceeds, so a slash that reaches frozen grant principal fails today) |\\n| Ghost Tasks: encrypted issuance + known-answer correctness canary | LIVE |\\n| Emission/halving/subsidy/committee premium | LIVE |\\n| Reward liquidity on issue (\u00a79.1 R9.13) | LIVE (validator earnings and sponsored-stake payouts are liquid, like the miner leg and the Labs/Foundation subsidy; earnings do not grow stake or its freeze. The agent and staker legs accrue in pool accounts until E.40 ratifies their distribution. The +9%/year baseline, capped at 1% of issuance, and `max(baseline, ValueCoupledStakeFloor)` eligibility floor remain independent: unchanged stake can fall below the growing floor) |\\n| Tx-fee split (10 burn / 90 author live; 80/10/10 target) | PARTIAL |\\n| Survival governor (both dampers) | PARTIAL (default OFF) |\\n\\n### H.5 HTLC, invariants, sessions, governance, validators (\u00a710\u2013\u00a715)\\n\\n| Requirement / mechanism | Status |\\n|-------------------------|--------|\\n| FLOP-leg HTLC create/redeem/refund; cross-chain pair profiles | LIVE local mechanics; all implemented pair directions target-only \u2014 conformance PENDING E.48 |\\n| Finality-safe FLOP refund; permissioned FLOP relayer gate | LIVE local mechanics; pair-level binding/finality PENDING E.48 |\\n| Agent-economics invariants (INV-02, INV-S01 session nonce, INV-M06 payout atomicity) | LIVE for INV-02 and INV-S01; INV-M06 PARTIAL (the burn leg's result is not checked); `fail_task` removed with the per-task path |\\n| INV-S03 pallet allowlist; INV-S05 immediate revocation | LIVE: direct calls checked; known runtime dispatch wrappers rejected for every session; revocation immediate |\\n| Session `G_n` plausibility gate + authenticated submitted-turn sum | LIVE arithmetic/authentication; execution guarantee GAP (E.43/E.44) |\\n| Current-profile channel payment without public work credit (R11.2b) | LIVE payment-only; future audited credit and historical recovery OPEN (E.44) |\\n| Sessions: cooperative path has 2 primary inclusions; variable turn/path/evidence cost; reserved capacity | LIVE mechanics; capacity mechanism PENDING; serialized bytes PARTIAL; withdrawal PROPOSED (ratification pending); benchmark/network GAP (E.44/E.46) |\\n| Terminal DA-loss settlement (R13.0c / V4) | GAP: receipt payout in code conflicts with D-0430 full-refund rule; a missing tariff now rejects (`SettlementTariffMissing`) except for a pre-v2 legacy channel, which the migration flag converts once |\\n| Failed/early-close three-way split (`\u03c6`) | LIVE |\\n| Dispute standing (agent + validators) | LIVE |\\n| Recursive dispute bisection beyond single turn | LIVE: on-chain midpoint rounds over complete power-of-two settled bundles; other bundles use single-turn `open_dispute` |\\n| Market-actor collusion detector + mechanism perturbation (R12.3) | PARTIAL: off-chain detector and dry-run perturbation canary LIVE; mechanism action open |\\n| Attestation-outage scoped pause (R13.0e / O1) | PLANNED: designed, not built |\\n| Session re-attestation cadence + max-duration extension | PLANNED |\\n| Per-task path removal | LIVE |\\n| OpenGov + `protocol_upgrade` (Root) track; Foundation submit gate; de-sudo | LIVE (de-sudo genesis-time) |\\n| Validator onboarding/duties/rotation | LIVE (stake-ordering PARTIAL; small-set ejection open, E.56) |\\n| Validator slashing table | LIVE (correlated equivocation curve PARTIAL) |\\n| V6 censorship (FOCIL); V8 ghost-task accountability; O3 attestation reputation; P3 provenance; A8 account recovery | PLANNED |\\n| Committee-sampling composition machine-check; PQ crypto | PARTIAL/OOS: committee gate predicate proved, including the bootstrap fallback; seat-capture composition PLANNED (E.42); quantum out of scope |\\n| Session capacity units (R11.2) | PARTIAL: source landed (elapsed-time bound; pre-open finality lag excluded); runtime qualification and deployment pending; the value-audit planner is SDK-only, with no production caller yet |\\n\\n**Regenerating the evidence-coverage matrix.** The per-section research/Lean/Quint/Julia backing is\\ngenerated separately into [`yellowpaper-coverage.md`](yellowpaper-coverage.md) via\\n`just yellowpaper-regen`.\\n\\n**Per-requirement attribution.** A finer, requirement-level map (each `R-id` \u2192 its Lean theorem / Quint\\ninvariant / Rust code path) is kept in the companion index\\n[`yellowpaper-attribution.md`](yellowpaper-attribution.md). It is non-normative and lives outside the\\nspec by design \u2014 it exposes proof-artifact and code-path detail the normative body omits.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Appendix I \u2014 Runtime Composition\\n\\nThe `construct_runtime!` inventory (source: `pallets/runtime/zkverify/src/lib.rs`). **Pallet indices are\\nconsensus- and encoding-critical:** they prefix every dispatch and storage key, so an index change is a\\nbreaking runtime upgrade requiring a migration (\u00a714.1). Indices are stable identifiers, not a sequence \u2014\\ngaps are intentional (removed pallets are not reused). This appendix is normative for the index values.\\n\\n**Core / system**\\n\\n| Idx | Pallet | Role |\\n|----:|--------|------|\\n| 0 | `frame_system` | base runtime |\\n| 1 \u00b7 2 | `scheduler` \u00b7 `preimage` | governance enactment / timelock / large-call storage (\u00a714) |\\n| 3 | `timestamp` | block time |\\n| 4 | `balances` | token accounts; existential deposit (\u00a76.5) |\\n| 5 | `transaction_payment` | fee model (\u00a74.2, \u00a79) |\\n\\n**Consensus**\\n\\n| Idx | Pallet | Role |\\n|----:|--------|------|\\n| 6 | `authorship` | block author note |\\n| 8 \u00b7 9 | `offences` \u00b7 `session_historical` | offence reports / historical session proofs (slashing, \u00a711) |\\n| 10 \u00b7 11 \u00b7 13 | `babe` \u00b7 `session` \u00b7 `authority_discovery` | BABE authoring; session keys; peer discovery (\u00a72) |\\n| 104 | `aleph` | AlephBFT committee snapshot + `LastFinalized` \u2192 `FinalizedPrefix` (\u00a72, \u00a715.4) |\\n\\n*Removed (D-0408): `pallet_staking` (was 7) and `bags_list` (was 19) \u2014 `validators` (96) is the sole\\nauthority source (\u00a76.1).*\\n\\n**Governance & utility**\\n\\n| Idx | Pallet | Role |\\n|----:|--------|------|\\n| 14 | `treasury` | on-chain treasury (\u00a714) |\\n| 15 \u00b7 16 \u00b7 17 | `conviction_voting` \u00b7 `referenda` \u00b7 `custom_origins` | OpenGov (\u00a714.1\u2013\u00a714.2) |\\n| 25 \u00b7 26 | `bounties` \u00b7 `child_bounties` | treasury bounties |\\n| 30\u201333 | `utility` \u00b7 `multisig` \u00b7 `proxy` \u00b7 `identity` | batching; multisig (\u00a76.1); proxy delegation (\u00a76.1); identity |\\n| 99 \u00b7 105 | `emergency_override` \u00b7 `emergency_pause` | break-glass + circuit breaker (\u00a714.1 R14.6) |\\n\\n**Bootstrap (removed at mainnet genesis handoff)**\\n\\n| Idx | Pallet | Role |\\n|----:|--------|------|\\n| 50 | `sudo` | bootstrap Root; **neutered + removed** at de-sudo (\u00a714.1 R14.3/R14.5) |\\n| 51 | `vesting` | generic vesting; removable once vesting completes |\\n\\n**FLOP protocol**\\n\\n| Idx | Pallet | Role \u00b7 spec \u00a7 |\\n|----:|--------|---------------|\\n| 81 | `aggregate` | verified-statement Merkle roots for cross-chain dispatch (\u00a73.6) |\\n| 83 \u00b7 84 | `token_claim` \u00b7 `crl` | airdrop claims \u00b7 certificate revocation |\\n| 85 | `has_station` | HTLC + predicate escrow (\u00a710) |\\n| 86 | `flop_poui` | PoUI proof verification, validator attestation, `flop_meter` (\u00a73.6, \u00a74) |\\n| 87 | `hw_calibration` | aggregate host calibration cap + renewable lease (\u00a77) |\\n| 88 \u00b7 91 | `work_vesting` \u00b7 `airdrop_vesting` | `R_p\u00b2` performance vesting (\u00a78) \u00b7 airdrop vesting (\u00a79) |\\n| 89 | `synthetic_tasks` | Ghost Tasks \u2014 liveness + correctness canary (\u00a78.1) |\\n| 90 | `attest` | shared attestation-profile registry (\u00a73.6) |\\n| 92 \u00b7 93 | `block_rewards` \u00b7 `flop_subsidy` | emission split (\u00a79) \u00b7 era-0 Labs/Foundation subsidy (\u00a79) |\\n| 94 \u00b7 95 \u00b7 106 | `session_keys` \u00b7 `agent_wallet` \u00b7 `agent_identity` | agent delegation + caps + circuit breaker (\u00a76.2) |\\n| 96 \u00b7 97 \u00b7 98 \u00b7 100 | `validators` \u00b7 `miner_staking` \u00b7 `delegation_cap` \u00b7 `miner_slashing` | validator authority + rotation + slashing (\u00a715); miner stake + delegation cap + slashing (\u00a76.1, \u00a711) |\\n| 101 \u00b7 102 \u00b7 103 | `model_registry` \u00b7 `da_registry` \u00b7 `compute_channel` | measured roots + decode-policy pins (\u00a73.3); sovereign DA (\u00a75.3); sessions (\u00a712) |\\n| 107 | `metering_verifier` | metering-certificate verification (\u00a74, E.34) |\\n\\n**Settlement verifiers** (`160\u2013170`) \u2014 **zkVerify aggregation, not inference proofs** (\u00a73.6):\\n`common` (160), `groth16` (161), `risc0` (162), `ultraplonk` (163), `plonky2` (165), `fflonk` (166),\\n`sp1` (167), `ultrahonk` (168), `ezkl` (169), `tee` (170).\\n\",\"lastModified\":null},{\"source\":\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/flop-labs/yellowpaper/70e691c758e53eed17a016a02b0a2ae1200d3744/CHANGELOG.md\",\"status\":200,\"measuredAt\":\"2026-11-06T03:27:25.293Z\",\"body\":\"# Yellowpaper changelog\\n\\nThe initial public release is **0.5.0 (draft)**. No version has been published yet. Prepublication\\nedits are folded into the initial text; there are no public errata or patch releases to record.\\nAfter publication, use Semantic Versioning and Keep a Changelog, preserving released versions.\\n\\n## [Unreleased]\\n\\n### Changed\\n\\n- Name RTMR3 as the only accepted measurement path for the model root (\u00a73.3 step 2), matching the\\n  step 3 verifier and D-0404.\\n\\n- Bring Appendix E/H status, trackers and code paths up to date with landed code; no protocol rule\\n  changes. Index the on-chain bisection dispute calls in G.1 and correct `open_dispute`'s arguments;\\n  mark multi-round bisection and `G_n` overflow rejection LIVE; record the development-network\\n  paid-storage pallet (rent released without audit), its CI-run Quint models and its simulation as\\n  PARTIAL; narrow E.9, E.32, E.41, E.46, E.47, E.51 and E.54 to what remains open; and replace\\n  enforcement paths for code removed with the per-task path in \u00a711.1 and H.5.\\n\\n- Specify Appendix D's chain inclusion-fee terms, align the shared-collateral example with its\\n  generated four-claim row, and list both work-vesting grant entry points in Appendix G.3.\\n\\n- Ratify slot/tranche position rent (D-0524, R5.4e/f, E.54, F.7, G.4): replacements retain\\n  historical earned rent, failed or forfeited deltas refund the payer, and new tariffs use separate\\n  funded tranches. Supersede independent provider ceilings; add seven executable balance vectors.\\n\\n- Dispose implemented HTLC pair directions as target-only for initial publication (E.48, #1498).\\n  Preserve cross-leg late-claim, finality-stall and failed-payout counterexamples, qualify the local\\n  formal models, and add focused pallet/contract expiry-ordering tests and a reproducible pair gate.\\n\\n- Specify the Agent airdrop unlock as spend-to-unlock (R8.7, R8.8; D-0522). An Agent grant unlocks\\n  nothing at its start and has no end block; it unlocks one FLOP per three FLOP of its locked\\n  principal in the gross `payable` of settled sessions, once every fraud dispute raised in the window has\\n  resolved, and its locked compute spend is capped at three quarters of principal. Channel escrow\\n  drawn from locked principal goes to the `payable` first and is refunded first, back to the grant as frozen\\n  principal. E.38 no longer holds the Agent horizon.\\n\\n- Make current-profile channel settlements payment-only (R11.2b, task 1494). Receipt claims no\\n  longer feed public work rewards or performance vesting, including unilateral/DA-void payout.\\n  Historical reco"
